# OCR Service - Invoice Test Data .gitignore

# Exclude binary invoice document files from version control to prevent repository bloat
# These files should be obtained separately and placed in this directory for testing
# This approach keeps the repository size manageable while ensuring test data consistency

# Document formats - All common invoice file formats
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.tiff
*.TIFF
*.tif
*.TIF
*.png
*.PNG
*.jpg
*.JPG
*.jpeg
*.JPEG
*.bmp
*.BMP
*.webp
*.WEBP

# Exclude generated OCR output files
# These are generated during testing and should not be committed
# Each developer should generate their own output files for comparison
output/*.txt
output/*.json
output/*.csv
output/*.xml

# However, we DO want to track the expected output files for validation
!expected/*.txt
!expected/*.json
!expected/*.csv
!expected/*.xml

# Exceptions - Track these specific files
!README.md
!config.json
!metadata.json
!sample_list.txt
!directory_structure.md
!expected_results.json
!test_manifest.json
!.gitkeep

# Temporary files that might be created during testing
*~
*.tmp
*.temp
*.log

# Instructions for obtaining test documents:
# 1. Download the invoice test dataset from the shared storage location:
#    s3://mca-documents-staging/test-data/invoices/
# 2. Place the files in this directory
# 3. Run the verification script to ensure all required test files are present:
#    python ../../verify_test_data.py --type invoices
#
# Note: The test_manifest.json file contains checksums and metadata for all required
# test documents. The verification script will use this to validate your test data.